msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-power-module.rst:79
#: db6e2220b2634c249923dc449d891d79
msgid "Extending Current Measurement Capacity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-power-module.rst:81
#: a0cb0fb1584a46bdb3eb058162bb2b16
msgid "Shunt resistor power monitors of this variety can be used to measure higher currents if setup in a current sharing configuration, as shown below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-power-module.rst:86
#: 4c94fa190b164e2f82ac68f09cd32aea
msgid "Design points:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-power-module.rst:88
#: 81204293ee294f78ac9b9d775a611538
msgid "The shunt should be approximately the same resistance as the power module. For example, a 120A module usually uses a 0.5 milliohm sense resistor. Therefore the wire shunt should be ~ 0.5 milliohm for equal sharing of the total current. This can be determined from a reference such as `this <https://www.engineeringtoolbox.com/wire-gauges-d_419.html>`_ . For 12ga wire, that would be ~ 4 inches."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-power-module.rst:89
#: dc25f2e9487949b79dd30128aeb62d9b
msgid "The wire gauge (and, of course, the wire used to connect the power module) should be rated to handle the expected continuous current for the length of wiring utilized."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-power-module.rst:90
#: 9a6ca7f093754931a6adfff2533314df
msgid "Try to keep the leads from the shunt junctions to power module short. Longer leads to the module there will increase resistance in that branch. This will unbalance the current split. Not an large issue, but will effectively increase the max resistance capability and decrease the incremental sensitivity of the measurement more than needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-power-module.rst:96
#: f2c45808de2043c689c86f8a95b41493
msgid "In the photo above, by providing two bypasses, the current is shared such that the power monitor sees a little less than 1/3 the total current flowing, and reports a value ~1/3 normal, extending its range ~3X."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-power-module.rst:98
#: 106e21921c7f46c1ac525fc353122556
msgid "Due to variations in materials, length, etc. it is mandatory that the monitor be calibrated using a precision current meter of some kind. It is best to calibrate at a value greater than 50% of the maximum current expected."
msgstr ""
